# OpenShift overrides — layered ON TOP of .env, never instead of it.
# ============================================================================
# Every script that targets the cluster reads BOTH files, .env first:
#
#     --env-file .env --env-file .env.openshift
#
# and the last definition of a repeated key wins, exactly as up.sh already
# layers the app's .env under this directory's. So the backend's address, the
# share root, the archive directory, the collector's uid/gid, the Artifactory
# registries — all of it is INHERITED, and stays correct in one place for both
# deployments. Only what the cluster genuinely changes belongs here.
#
# What the cluster changes is one thing: DNA is served under a path prefix
# beside the other ShotGrid tools on sg.spimageworks.com, rather than owning
# the root of its own host.
# ============================================================================

# Where the app is mounted. TWO halves that must agree:
#
#   VITE_BASE_PATH   build time — Vite bakes it into every asset URL and
#                    re-exposes it as import.meta.env.BASE_URL, which is what
#                    src/basePath.ts reads to prefix the addresses the BACKEND
#                    builds (a recording's media_url, a review link's url_path).
#                    Trailing slash, because that is what Vite's `base` wants.
#
#   APP_BASE_PATH    run time — envsubst puts it in front of every nginx
#                    location. NO trailing slash: the locations supply it.
#
# Setting one without the other is the failure worth knowing about: matching
# base paths are what make the SPA's own asset URLs and nginx's locations
# describe the same address. Left unset both are empty, which is the root-served
# deployment and the upstream default.
VITE_BASE_PATH=/dna/
APP_BASE_PATH=/dna

# The API is reached at the same prefix — nginx strips it before proxying to
# BACKEND_URL, so the backend is unaware it is being served under one.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/dna/api

# Follow Along's session directory, likewise proxied from under the prefix.
VITE_FOLLOW_ALONG_SESSIONS_URL=/dna/review-sessions

# NOT set here, deliberately: VITE_WS_URL. It stays empty (from .env) so the
# app derives the socket from the page origin AND the base path — see the
# warning in .env.example. A value here would be baked in absolute and could
# not follow the mount.
